# Supply-chain hardening — applied 2026-05-25 in response to ongoing
# Shai-Hulud / Mini Shai-Hulud / TeamPCP waves (active campaign throughout
# 2025-09 → 2026-05). See SECURITY.md "Supply-chain defense layers".

# Disable lifecycle scripts (postinstall / preinstall / install) by default.
# These were the primary execution vector in the original Shai-Hulud worm.
# We explicitly do not need any package's install-time scripts at this repo
# (no native compilation, no binary downloads).
ignore-scripts=true

# 7-day cooldown — refuse to install any package version published less than
# 10080 minutes (= 7 days) ago. Historical compromised waves are typically
# yanked from the registry within 24-72 hours of detection, so a 7-day window
# absorbs essentially all known supply-chain attack lifetimes (e.g. axios
# March 2026 = 4-5 hours; Shai-Hulud TanStack May 11 = 22 min publishing
# burst).
#
# Cited primary source: pnpm 10.16 (2025-09) shipped minimumReleaseAge.
# pnpm 11.0 ships this gate ON by default at 1440 (1 day); we raise it to
# 7 days to match the broader 2026 industry recommendation.
minimum-release-age=10080

# Audit-time floor: fail `pnpm audit` on any high-or-critical advisory.
audit-level=high
